# Marketing routes are real files (wallet.html, terms.html …), and Pages
# serves those at their extensionless path on its own — /portal reaches
# portal.html with no rule here. The payment page is one of them: a customer
# opening a link on mobile data should not download the whole app to read an
# account number.
#
# There is deliberately no /pay rule. Pages answers /pay.html with a 308 to
# /pay, so rewriting /pay to /pay.html made the two redirect at each other and
# the payment page never loaded at all.

# The homepage is the static landing page (web/landing/), not the Flutter app.
# It loads in one request on mobile data; the app still owns every other path.
/    /landing/    200

# Anything else belongs to the Flutter app.
/*    /index.html    200
